  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Design Concepts**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to visualize this web application. The initial task is translating the user\'s intent to create an app with specific screens, referencing an image and HTML provided. I am planning to use direct links, likely focusing on how to structure the web app and how to derive the screens based on the information provided.\n\n\n**Defining Screen Structure**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the screen structure based on the \"Supervisi\303\263n\" dashboard image. The left sidebar, top header elements like the title, badges, and user profile, plus the subheader navigation tabs (\"Monitoreo de usuarios,\" etc.) are the initial focus. My key attention is on how these elements create the app\'s overall structure. I\'m noting the main workspace with the text, the filters, and the data table.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Rows**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of each data row, dissecting the column details. I\'m focusing on the \"Nombres y Apellidos\", \"Estado\", \"M\303\263dulo\", and data metrics (\"Tickets activos,\" \"Estrategias activas,\" etc.).  I\'m noting how each row presents its data, like the inclusion of icons and dynamic call details, and how the various agent states affect the presentation of data. I\'m taking special care regarding the different modules and their respective data displays.\n\n\n**Expanding Interaction Elements**\n\nI\'m now expanding the interactive elements to create a high-fidelity, functional supervision dashboard. I\'m focusing on adding and editing agents, changing their statuses with visual updates, and implementing dynamic table filtering by search text, status, company, or campaign. I\'ll also add mockups for the dialpad, detailed call views, simulation controls, and a webphone toggle, as well as tabs.\n\n\n**Incorporating New Dashboard Elements**\n\nI\'m excited about integrating the \"Colas\" queue monitoring, \"Grabaciones\" call recordings, and \"Calidad\" call evaluation features. They fit the layout perfectly! I am now thinking about how these elements will appear on the design. The integration opens up possibilities; I\'m considering adding an \"Asistente IA para Supervisi\303\263n\" panel to tap into the Gemini API for summaries and recommendations.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 229776927
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
