    thinking: "**Updating Metadata and Name**\n\nI\'m focusing on naming the application and updating the `metadata.json` file. Considering the existing HTML title, I\'ve decided on \"Supervisi\303\263n Score Cloud\" or \"Gotravel Dashboard - Supervisi\303\263n\" as names. The goal is a literal and descriptive name, especially since this is a focused application.\n\n\n**Refining App Name & Features**\n\nI\'ve settled on \"Supervisi\303\263n Score Cloud\" as the application name, aiming for directness and clarity matching the page\'s content. Now, I\'m exploring potential features, including a \"Supervisor AI Assistant\" sidebar leveraging simulated or API-driven smart analysis using Gemini. I want to ensure the AI integration is optional, prioritizing a user-friendly experience regardless of API key configuration.\n\n\n**Considering API Key Handling**\n\nI\'m thinking about gracefully handling API keys, specifically the Gemini API. The challenge is balancing server-side security with client-side interactivity. The potential for a server-side app to enable Gemini API integration is now very clear to me. However, I am now thinking a client-side SPA with simulated AI behavior might be a better approach, given the user request for an interactive UI showcase and considering I am not obligated to use the API at all.\n\n\n"
